{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 160,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a video of light traveling through \na bottle at 250 billion frames per second. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6000,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And here's that same video. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7840,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now with the camera moving. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13200,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see it sweeps across the scene \nfaster than the laser pulse itself, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17520,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means this camera must be \ntraveling faster than light. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21440,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how is this possible? "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24400,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, in this video, I wanna show you \nthree unusual ways of stopping time "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28960,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what you can see if \nyou just keep slowing down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32240,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From a century old technique that \nstill beats modern slow-mo cameras,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35480,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " as all the way to a massive \nquadrillion frames per second camera "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39200,
    "dDurationMs": 3325,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that captures electrons \nwhizzing around molecules. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48160,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the 1920s, electric motors were the new \nstandard for powering factories and mills, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54320,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but many of these motors also came with a flaw. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57600,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were sensitive to fluctuations \nin the electrical grid. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61120,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A power surge, like from a lightning \nstrike made them behave unpredictably. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65920,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So one MIT engineer named Harold \"Doc' \nEdgerton, set out to find a solution. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73760,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He had a setup that could induce these power \nsurges in a lab, but no matter what he tried, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78960,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Edgerton just couldn't see what was \ngoing on with the motors because the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "machines would spin too fast \nfor the human eye to see. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86400,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And cameras at the time offered no help. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89360,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their exposure times were too slow,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91680,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so any photograph of a running \nmotor would come out blurry. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But one day, Edgerton noticed that \nevery time he triggered a power surge,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101120,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his equipment gave off a bright flash of light. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103920,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when that flash hit the motor,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105600,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the moving parts appeared to stand \nperfectly still as if frozen in time, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111520,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which gave him an idea. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113520,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He could turn off all the lights in the room, \nset up a camera, and leave the shutter open. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since there was no light, no \nimage would form on the film. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122960,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then if he could illuminate the motor \nwith a very brief and very bright flash,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127920,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the ones his equipment gave off, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129840,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well then he would get a sharp photograph. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133360,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All Edgerton needed was a way to \nreliably create these flashes. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138320,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So he started by using a high voltage \npower source to load electrons onto a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142480,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "capacitor where they piled \nup onto one of the plates. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145360,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because there was an insulator \nslotted between the two sides,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148240,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the electrons couldn't just jump to the \npositive side to balance out the charges. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152560,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only way for them to get there would be \nto travel through the rest of the circuit. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156640,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the circuit was intentionally designed so \nthat electrons would have to cross a glass tube "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161680,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "filled with a non conducting \ngas like argon or xenon. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165760,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On their own they would not have \nthe energy to get through that gas. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169520,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Edgerton added a trigger that sent a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172000,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "high voltage pulse through a \nwire wrapped around the tube"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176080,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the electric field from that pulse would rip \nelectrons off the gas atoms inside the chamber,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181040,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ionizing the gas and turning it into a conductor. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184000,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In that instant, the charge stored in \nthe capacitor would surge through heating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the gas to around 10,000 Kelvin, nearly \ntwice as hot as the surface of the Sun. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193360,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This would produce a very bright, very brief \nflash of light lasting just 10 microseconds. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199520,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then the electrons would recombine with the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201440,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gas atoms stopping the current and \nthe circuit would go dark again. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205360,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was Edgerton's strobe. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209200,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the early 1930s, he was eager \nto test it outside the lab,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213120,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so he packed up a strobe and \nhit the road with his wife. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217120,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When he saw a random factory, he \npulled over, got inside the nearest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221360,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "phone booth and called up the factory's \npresident and asked him something like: "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225120,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Do you happen to have any \nmotors in there that don't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227840,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "work right? I'd like to show you something.\" "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230640,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More often than not, he ended up inside setting \nup the strobe next to one of the motors. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235360,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The workers would watch as \nEdgerton froze the motor in time,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238880,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "allowing them to take sharp \npictures of the gears in motion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242720,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Edgerton isn't the first to make a \nstrobe. Rather he took new bits of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246560,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "technology that existed so he \ncould make a better strobe. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A strobe that was brighter, shorter flash \nduration. But he was not unique in that. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253360,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There were lots of electrical engineers in the \nworld at that time who could have done that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257920,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, what Edgerton uniquely brought to \nthe table was his eye for photography."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262400,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He took photos of synchronous motors,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I think in part because he just \nthought synchronous motors were cool. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267760,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One day he showed his wife the 300th photo \nof a synchronous motor. And she said, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273280,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Harold, can't you take a picture of \nsomething a little more interesting?\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277680,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so he did. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tennis balls, pancaked against the \nracket, hummingbirds frozen in time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286880,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was one of the first to really \nstart using strobes to communicate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291280,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what's happening at these \ntimescales we can't see. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294400,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He would do this through like \"Life \nMagazine,\" \"National Geographic, magazines. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298240,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These magazines in the '30's, '40's,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300480,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were essentially the social \nmedia influencers of the day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303600,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He just had this eye for composition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306880,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most of these pictures were \ntaken in the 1930s and yeah,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310160,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it seems easy enough to swing a racket and it's \neasy enough to press a button on the strobe, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but how do you time the strobe to go off \nexactly as the racket hits the tennis ball?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320400,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the million dollar question, right? "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322160,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have a strobe that turns on and off and \nhalf a millionth of the second, that's nice. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325680,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How do you get it to go off to the right half  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327680,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "millionth of the second? 'Cause \nthere are a lot of them right? "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331200,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the answer is we use sound."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333680,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we're gonna try and recreate \none of Edgerton's photos,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336880,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "popping a balloon and freezing it in time. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339440,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is it okay if we walk through the setup?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341520,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think that would make perfect sense. \nWhy don't you blow up a balloon. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344560,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Step one is you set up the experiment, \nor in this case, the performer. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348640,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the next thing you \nwanna do is frame the image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350720,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So you're framing now before the \nballoon pops to get focus and things?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354400,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Exactly, if you can't get a good \nphoto with nothing happening,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358400,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "adding the motion will not help. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360000,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so the next step will be to \nget the strobe in the right spot. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364240,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the strobe is set up with a \ntrigger unit with a microphone. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368640,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when a sharp sound hits the microphone,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371360,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the trigger unit sends a \nsignal to set off the strobe. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374960,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're gonna turn the lights out and then \nwe're gonna open the shutter of the camera,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379360,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but there won't be an image \nbecause the room will be dark. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382400,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I'll say three, two, one, pop. And when I \nsay pop, pop the balloon with an upward motion. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 387200,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when the sound from the pop hits the mic, \nafter a minor delay, the strobe will fire. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The camera will capture that image for \nthe one 100,000th of a second it's lit. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397600,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alright, we ready? "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399280,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lights out please. And three, two, one, pop. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404240,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lights. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405360,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, there you go. Oh, you look hmmmm. \nDo not mess with this man. Nope."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409600,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh, it's awesome. You can see inside the balloon. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412000,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's really cool. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414160,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is another image we took. Can you guess \nwhat this is? This hovering white orb. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419360,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's another photo just a moment later. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421760,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like a little sombrero!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423440,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is, yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424960,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That orb is a drop of milk falling onto a plate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428320,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's a pancake. But you'll notice \nthe little drops are all spreading out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432240,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, it's so, so crisp."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434160,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Come around and have a look here. Right, it's \ntranslucent here. You're seeing through it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438320,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, wow. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440000,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, once Edgerton showed the world \nhow powerful strobe photography was,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444160,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he attracted some unexpected attention. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446800,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1939, a US major named George Goddard \nwalked into Edgerton's lab unannounced. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453040,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was working in the Army's photographic lab,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455520,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "developing ways to photograph enemy \nmovements from a plane during the nighttime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460160,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The old way of doing a night \nreconnaissance photograph was to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464400,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fly over the site at high altitude \nand drop a flare on a parachute. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469920,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then the reconnaissance plane \nhad to fly in under the flare  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474480,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where it would be silhouetted, \nwhere you could shoot at it. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477120,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Big problem..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478080,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right? So totally exposed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481120,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Goddard wanted a safer way. So \nhe asked Edgerton whether he  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484320,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could develop a strobe powerful \nenough to illuminate the ground"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487200,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from a plane that was a mile or so \nup in the sky. A strobe that would  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491280,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be bright enough to take a reconnaissance photo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493760,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Edgerton pulled out some paper, \ndid a few calculations and said: "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497280,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"We can do that.\" "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498960,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The flash released about 60,000 \njoules in a single millisecond. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503280,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A peak power of roughly 60 megawatts, which is \ncomparable to the output of a large solar farm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508800,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One, two, three, push."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512320,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The flash lamp was quickly \nutilized in World War II and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515440,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it allowed the allies to take pictures \nof Normandy the night before D-Day. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519600,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This way they could confirm that German \ntroops were unprepared for the attack. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524400,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's hard to ignore just how \nsharp these strobe photos are,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527680,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially the ones Edgerton took in the 1930s. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530720,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we got a research grade slow-mo camera from \n2020 that shoots at 20,000 FPS, and we're gonna  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537440,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compare its quality to Edgerton's technique \nby shooting a bullet through a playing card. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542720,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's do the slow-mo camera first."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544720,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Three, two, one. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547440,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's see the video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550160,
    "dDurationMs": 5517,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, it's great to see how long the top \npart, which is now levitating, it stays up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 555677,
    "dDurationMs": 2563,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is now, yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561360,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, and now let's do the \nsame with Edgerton's method."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564160,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Light's going out. Shutter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568240,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Shutter open."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569200,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Three, two, one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572160,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, I think I saw it! That's cool. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579360,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The focus is amazing. The edge \nof the card is beautiful. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584160,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see this ghost effect? There's like card."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587280,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ah, you do see the ghost effect \nand that's because you open the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591040,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shutter and it was a second or two \nbefore I actually fired the gun. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594000,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's enough stray light in the room \nto give you a faint exposure there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597920,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also, we still used a microphone to time the \nbullet, even though it's faster than sound."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602960,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So here's the gun, it fires, \nthe sound of the gun comes out,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607040,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the bullet is coming out ahead of the sound, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610000,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the bullet is supersonic and a supersonic  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613920,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "object moving through the air \ncreates a sound, a sonic boom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618080,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now you can pick up that \nsonic boom with a microphone,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621040,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by moving the microphone \nphysically along the trajectory,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624800,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get the time where the bullet is \ngonna be when the strobe goes off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 628320,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think it's a brilliant way to solve the problem \nand I get to say that because I did not invent it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634320,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Edgerton was very inventive and \nhad projects all over the place. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637760,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He was teaching at MIT, but then \nhe had companies for things like  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641600,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "underwater cameras and he was making movies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 643600,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and oh, he even won an Oscar. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if there's anything he wanted \nto do, he sort of just did it. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649280,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I feel like I'm quite the opposite. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651600,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, when I joined Veritasium back \nin 2023, I started off as a researcher. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655360,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I was fact checking videos and setting up shoots,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657840,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but then Derek and the other writers \nsuggested I should make a video of my own. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661600,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I remember thinking, yeah, \nI don't know, maybe one day. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665200,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they kept pushing for me to do it. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666800,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I'm so glad that they did because \nwhen Derek and I made my first video,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 670720,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I fell in love with it. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672000,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if there's anything you're putting \noff, you should just go do it. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675280,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if that something is a project you want \nto set up as an entrepreneur or a creator,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679920,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, today's sponsor Hostinger, \nmakes that first step really simple. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683200,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Say you need a website or a store \nor any kind of online presence, H"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686960,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ostinger is an all-in-one AI-powered ecosystem \nthat will get you up and running within minutes. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691840,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With Hostinger you don't need any kind of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693760,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crazy tech skills. It's all \nfrictionless and affordable. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696240,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can go from an idea to execution \nwithout needing 10 apps on your computer. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700960,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If there's a project you've been \nputting off for that 'one day',  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703760,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turn that into your 'day one' with Hostinger. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706320,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Head to hostinger.com/Veritasium10 \nand use our code Veritasium to get  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710480,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "10% off your subscription. You \ncan also scan QR code here. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714320,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I want to thank Hostinger \nfor sponsoring this part of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716720,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the video. And now let's go look \nat pictures of that card we shot. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720560,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So here are the two techniques side-by-side, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722720,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and here's Edgerton's original as well. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726240,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why does a research grade \ncamera from 2020 struggle to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728960,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get the same resolution as \na camera from decades ago? "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732400,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because we are really \nworking with two resolutions here. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735120,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A spatial resolution or how \nmany pixels your image has, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738480,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a temporal resolution which dictates whether \nyou only capture one frame, like a strobe photo "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743600,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or a progression of frames \nlike our high speed video. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747040,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem is that more often than not,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749200,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the hardware is limited so that you really \nhave to trade one resolution for the other. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753440,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "High pixel count or high frame rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756320,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The fundamental limit you hit is how \nfast you can get pixels off the sensor. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759680,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's why there's a maximum speed to \nread every pixel and then to go any faster,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765040,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you have to not read out all the pixels. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767280,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this camera will give you \na million frames a second,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but you're like 16 by 128 pixels. \nAnd that's not much of a image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775040,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so there's always this trade off. Either you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777280,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "go for very high pixel counts \nand bring the frame rate down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780400,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the Edgerton Center we pushed this as far \nas it goes with one frame and that's it. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784640,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you can also push it the other way, one \npixel and very high FPS. 1 trillion FPS in fact. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792240,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But wait, it's just one pixel. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794240,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What can you do with one pixel? "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796640,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Great question. In the cameras that I can \nshow you today are cameras that you're right,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800720,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they can really only see one pixel at a time, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802800,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they can see close to a trillion \nframes per second. And what that lets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807680,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you do is ultra slow motion videos \nshowing light actually traveling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 811360,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's that video of light traveling \nthrough a bottle. You can see the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815920,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wavefronts that form below the bottle and \neven how the light bounces off the cap. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821760,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And even though this looks like a normal video,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can take it with a camera \nthat only sees one pixel. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827280,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here's how you do it. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828320,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A single pixel camera is one that captures just \none thing, how many photons land on the sensor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834160,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the sensor here is typically sensitive enough \nto register whether even a single photon hits it. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839360,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it can count those incoming photons \naround a trillion times a second. So each bin,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and technically each frame is \nroughly one picosecond long. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849040,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In that time, even light itself \ntravels only 0.3 millimeters. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854720,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sounds impressive, but we've actually had  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856400,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this tech in many phones for \nyears now. It's just LIDAR. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859520,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You shoot out a pulse of light,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861200,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it bounces off and you time how long \nit takes for that pulse to come back. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 864800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And from that you get the distance to \nthe object that it bounced off of. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 868400,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this is all you need to \ntake a speed of light video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871280,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have a setup here that is basically a scaled  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873440,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down room. And we just have \nsome different shapes in it. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876240,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have a cone of sphere, we have \na mirror in the back. And finally  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 880880,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have the Veritasium and \nthe Camera Culture logos.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884800,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We wanna see light propagating through a scene.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887920,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the way we do that is we shoot out a \nreally short laser pulse that hits just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 892000,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one point in the scene and that laser \npulse has a ton of photons in it.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895600,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those photons will hit an \nobject scatter everywhere,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898320,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we want to see what that scattering looks \nlike at all these portions of the scene.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902800,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To start, our single pixel camera \nwill point at the top left corner.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906560,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when a pack of photons from the laser \npulse hit this random spot on the wall,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910880,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reflect to the corner and \nfinally bounce into the camera,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914400,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sensor is gonna pick up their \nsignal at a trillion frames per second,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 918560,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that signal will be pretty faint."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922320,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the problem here is that we're \nexposing for such a short time that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925520,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you actually just don't get \nthat much photon return.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927680,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What we do is we actually take a bunch of \nmeasurements and then group them all together and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930880,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that gives us actual usable information about, you \nknow, how far away the light traveled in a scene."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936240,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you move the camera slightly \nand repeat the experiment.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939600,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you shoot out a laser pulse, you let it scatter  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941920,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off the same spot and record the \nsignal from this new position.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 945520,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can do that a couple hundred times and move  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 948080,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the camera again until you get a grid \nof points across the whole scene.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952640,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You're literally going just one pixel at a time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954960,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One pixel at a time. That's \nthe caveat. Yeah, exactly. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 957280,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We actually have two mirrors \nhere that let us steer the beam,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 961120,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know, left and right and up and down.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963200,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So by turning where the mirror is, \nwe can turn where the sensor looks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966800,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The most important thing for this \ntechnique to work is that the scene  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969680,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has to play out pretty much exactly the \nsame every time you move the sensor,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973520,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because if it didn't, then every \npixel will tell a different story.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977120,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like if I try to record this \nsection four separate times and use  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 980320,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a quarter of each to fill in the screen \nscreen, I would get a garbled mess.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984800,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thankfully the laser pulse in our \nscene scatters pretty predictably."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988960,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's what lets us get unlimited \nresolution. So we can basically say,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992400,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's scan as many points in the scene as we \nneed. That gives us good spatial resolution."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 997200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The more points you scan along this grid, the \nhigher your final resolution. If you want 4K,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1002000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you simply scan a 4K grid of pixels. \nIt's just gonna take more time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005840,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The nice thing is light is fast, so we can \ndo this as fast as the mirrors can move."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010560,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Within just a couple of minutes. \nThe sensor captures millions of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1013680,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "laser pulses across the whole grid.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016720,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is now everything compiled \ntogether for a time of flight?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019760,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Exactly, this is everything put together. So what  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1021760,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're looking at now is going to \nbe again for a fixed laser spot. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1025840,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I'm gonna click play."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1031760,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, Camera Culture logo!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1033520,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034320,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of this was less than \neight nanoseconds of time. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037440,
    "dDurationMs": 8480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And here's another scene under the same setup. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1045920,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now you can also take this \na step further by rotating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1048800,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the scene and recording multiple points of view."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1051840,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have this algorithm that kind \nof takes this Coke bottle video  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1056000,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "capture from different views and is \nable to create these fly-throughs,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060720,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "being able to see the light propagate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062160,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from any direction and like flying \nthrough the scene as it's happening."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1065200,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, that's so cool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1067120,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So some things that are interesting to note is – "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069200,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because we're moving towards the right and \nthe light is propagating towards the right,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1072480,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but we're moving kind of \nfaster in this visualization –"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075120,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this wavefront appears stationary, as you can see."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1078640,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh yeah. That is kind of breaking physics. I \nmean, you are moving the camera faster than light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083520,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, exactly, yeah it's kind \nof mind boggling almost. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1091280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is a fish tank that we put a \nmirror into and this diffuse reflector."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1096560,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you'll see a pulse of light \nwill enter the fish tank,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099360,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it will reflect off the mirror \nand hit the diffuse reflector."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1103760,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's crazy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105040,
    "dDurationMs": 4659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a diffraction grating. So it's kind of \ndefracts the light into different modes. So again,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1109699,
    "dDurationMs": 1501,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you see the light enter the tank and it \nseparates into these different modes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1111200,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those are the different modes? That's insane. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1114240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "My first impression was, oh, these are \njust simulations from I don't know,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1117760,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unreal Engine 5. But this is, like, real data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1120800,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like the bullet time video in \n\"Matrix.\" You've probably seen that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1123680,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No way! Is your motivation \"The Matrix?\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1126480,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the way, these videos were created \nat the University of Toronto and MIT, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1131760,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but Brian from AlphaPhoenix actually built one of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134880,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these speed of light cameras \nin his garage, which is mad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138400,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You should go check that out. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1139840,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So those are the two extremes. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1141520,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Strobe photography on one side \nand a trillion FPS on the other. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1145840,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you combine both, you actually \nget to see what electrons are doing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1152560,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though what that means exactly is debated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1156160,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You say electrons act like \nwaves? No, they don't exactly. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159520,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They act like particles. No, they don't exactly. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1162160,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can write mathematical expressions and \ncalculate what the thing is going to do. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1167840,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Without actually being able to picture it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1170000,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do electrons exist?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1172480,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How truthful do you want me to be?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1175040,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we still don't have a video or photo of \nelectrons, but this might be the next best thing. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1180640,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to pull it off, we had to build big, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1184400,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really big. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1187120,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, we're driving down what up until \n2017 was the world's straightest object. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1192800,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we've been driving for like \nwhat, five, five-ish minutes?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1195520,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, and we are wanna say about halfway there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1199520,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, I thought we were… Oh \nno, there's a lot more there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204320,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's do it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1206000,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's go see it. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1207760,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is SLAC, a US national lab \nthat houses a 3.2-kilometer-long,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1212240,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "perfectly straight electron accelerator. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1214880,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whoa. That is so long down there!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1217920,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that it just continues \nlike this all the way down it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1221600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The noise you hear is exactly 120 hertz. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1224800,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the frequency at which \nelectron pulses are generated  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1227600,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "underneath this building, 120 pulses a second. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1230640,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is the sound of the \nequipment that accelerates  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1233200,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them to over 99.9999992% the speed of light. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1239120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this lets you see electron clouds \nmove around molecules, essentially?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1244240,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right? So why would you care? "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1246320,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because essentially electrons create the \nfields in which everything else happens. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1252000,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Molecular bonds break and form because the \nelectrons essentially give them a push to do so. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1258800,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right, so the electrons are responsible \nfor everything that you see in nature "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1262720,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and being able to look into their motion  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1265200,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the most fundamental way of \nstudying materials and matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1269040,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, to achieve this, you need a \nnanoscopic equivalent of a strobe. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1273600,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you first feed these relativistic  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1275920,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electron pulses through a set \nof devices called undulators. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1279920,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're stacks of magnets spaced only a few \nmillimeters apart, with alternating poles. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285440,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the first pair has the north pole facing the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1287760,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electron pulse from above \nand the south from below. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1291440,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then the second pair flips and so on. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1294000,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now because the electrons are traveling through a \nmagnetic field, a force called the Lorentz force "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299040,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will push them in a direction perpendicular to \nboth their velocity and the magnetic field lines, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1304000,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in accordance with the left hand rule. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1306160,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So at one magnet pair, the \nelectrons will curve clockwise,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1309440,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and at the next pair counterclockwise and so on. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1312800,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This causes the electrons to wiggle. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1315280,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now since the electrons carry a charge,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1317600,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this wiggling motion causes them \nto emit electromagnetic radiation. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1321840,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And even though they oscillate at these millimeter \nwavelengths because of the magnet spacing, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1326480,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the wavelength of the resulting \nEM radiation is much smaller."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1330640,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the fun thing about \nthe theory of relativity. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1333120,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you would travel at near the speed \nof light, the length scales contract. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337920,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While that periodic structure \nis macroscopic for us,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1340880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right? We see each magnet, \nthese are centimeter scales. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1345840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the electron because it's traveling \nso fast, all of that space contracts. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1350640,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so it's actually oscillating \nreally, really fast. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1354720,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And these oscillation periods are compressed. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it means that if you compare that to \nwavelengths, that is in the x-ray domain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1362800,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that actually only gets your wavelength \npart of the way to the true x-ray regime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1367600,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if as an observer you stand at \nthe far end of the accelerator, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1372080,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all those electrons will be coming at \nyou at more than 99% the speed of light. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1376640,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in your reference frame, any light those \nelectrons emit will additionally be blueshifted,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1381760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "producing x-rays as small as \n50 picometers in wavelengths. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1386160,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Initially, these x-rays are created \nrandomly along the undulator,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1389920,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "producing an incoherent light pattern. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1392320,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But soon after, the electric fields from the \nx-rays start to interact with the electrons, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1398160,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "speeding some of them up and slowing others down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401520,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This causes faster electrons \nto catch up with slower ones. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1404880,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they get bunched up into periodic structures,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1408240,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "parallel sheets that are spaced at distances \nexactly equal to the wavelength of the X-rays. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1413680,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is called microbunching. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1415360,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now these sheets of electrons \nemit light as unified fronts. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1419040,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the resulting X-rays come \nout coherently as a laser  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1422320,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pulse. This dramatically increases their intensity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1426320,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the pulses come out incredibly tightly \npacked, being only a few femtoseconds long, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1432000,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they can get as short as \na couple hundred attoseconds. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1435280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's 10 to the power of negative \n18. An absurdly quick pulse. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1439840,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To put it another way, the attosecond is to the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1442720,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "second what the second is \nto the age of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1446640,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On an attosecond scale, you can see electrons \nzip around essentially atoms and molecules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1452000,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's insane. Yeah. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1453600,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After the undulators the x-ray pulses are sent to \nexperimental stations at the end of the tunnel. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1458880,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So where's the main x-ray beam?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1460960,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The main x-ray beam is coming \nthrough this tube over here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1463680,
    "dDurationMs": 320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1464000,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you wanted to... It's a little harder to \nsee, but coming in through this tube over here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1468080,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is the main place where \nthe x-rays come into the hutch. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1470800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so the x-rays focus into what \nwe call an interaction point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1475120,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now you fill this interaction point with the \nmolecules whose electrons you want to study."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1478960,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we shine that x-ray pulse on a molecule,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1481600,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when it hits the molecule, \nit will ionize the molecule "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1485360,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it ionizes predominantly from these \ninner shells from the very core parts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1491520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The thing is, core level electrons from different \nelements have different ionization energies. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1496400,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you want an x-ray to eject a \ncore level electron from a nitrogen,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500640,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it needs around 400 electron volts. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1503040,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whereas for an oxygen, it needs around 550. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1506640,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So by tuning the x-ray energy to \nmatch these ionization energies, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1510800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get to choose which of these atoms within \nthe molecule the x-ray is going to ionize. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1515920,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And any excess energy left after \nan x-ray has ejected an electron  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1520080,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will be taken by that electron as kinetic energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1523200,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, once you ionize this molecule,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1526720,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the kinetic energy will tell you something \nabout what's going on around that electron. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1531680,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, electrons are not independent \nparticles, they talk to each other, right? "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1535280,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have a negative charge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1537040,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you have a high electron \ndensity around a particular atom, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1540320,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the core level electrons will be \nbound less tightly to the nucleus "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1543920,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because of the presence of all these \nother electrons around the atom. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1547280,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So its ionization energy will \nactually be slightly lower. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1550400,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whereas if you have a lower electron \ndensity than average around an atom, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1554640,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those core level electrons will be bound more \ntightly with a higher ionization energy. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1559040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, when you measure the kinetic \nenergy of the electrons you eject, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1563040,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can use the difference between the input x-ray  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1565680,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy and the output kinetic energy to \ninfer what that electron density was."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1571120,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, once we can take a \npicture of an electron density,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1573680,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can change what the molecule is doing, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1575520,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make it do some process in time, and then we \ncan look at how electron densities change. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1580320,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have above us. We actually \nhave an entire laser hall. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1582880,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we generate laser light,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1584320,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we bring it down through tubes like here \nbehind you or over here on the ceiling."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1588480,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Traditional laser light. \nThese are infrared lasers. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1590800,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We bring them onto this table. And you \nsee all these boxes on this table? "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1594240,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These boxes are to condition laser to \ngive it the properties that we want."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1598080,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can change the color of the laser, \nwe can change the polarization state, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1602000,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can change the duration of the pulse. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1604080,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we sculpt these pulses, then we have them go \nco-propagating with the x-rays into our target. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1610320,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, now our first laser pulse will create \nsome non-equilibrium state in the molecule, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1616200,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will drive some dynamics and then \nour x-ray pulse will probe it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1619840,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This attosecond x-ray pulse ejects an electron \nfrom the molecule after a time delay t. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1625280,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And by measuring the kinetic \nenergy of the electron,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1628320,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can study how the electron density of \nthe molecule reacted to the trigger laser. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1633280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you get an attosecond snapshot, like \na strobe, of how the molecule changed. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1638320,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you can get another sample of the same \nmolecule, shoot it with a laser again, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1642640,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this time increase the probe \ndelay slightly to t plus delta t. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1647360,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This will tell you how the electron \ndensity changes a little later. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1651360,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you can keep increasing \nthis delay each time to get  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1654080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a sequence of snapshots of how that \nelectron density evolves over time. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1659600,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Isn't there a big assumption \nhere that every time you do it,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1662320,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're expecting a repeatable \nresult from the molecules?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1665080,
    "dDurationMs": 7080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, absolutely, so you need for your initiator \nto drive the same dynamics over and over again. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1672160,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you have a new process happening \nevery time, this technique will fail."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1676560,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if the scene is repeatable, \nthen like the trillion FPS camera,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1680240,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can use this technique \nto create a molecular movie. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1683280,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And here, the smallest amount by \nwhich you can tweak the time delay  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1686720,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for this x-ray strobe is around 300 attoseconds. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1690160,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can get frames that are only a \nfew hundred attoseconds seconds apart. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1694160,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you stitch those together,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1695600,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get a movie that technically runs \nat over a quadrillion frames per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1702640,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is a movie of the dynamics \nthat we might like to image. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1708400,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is a small molecular system. \nThis is called para-aminophenol. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1712880,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This calculation was done by some \nof our collaborators in Madrid. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1717600,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They had calculated what is the response of \nthis molecule to the removal of an electron. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1725200,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they simulate an x-ray pulse \ncoming in and removing an electron. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1730080,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the red color here represents an \nincrease in the density of the electron,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1734080,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the blue represents a decrease. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1736160,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so we see that when we've shined this x-ray  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1738960,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pulse onto this molecule and \nwe've removed an electron, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1742240,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we initiate some charge distribution \nthat starts to move across the molecule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1746480,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so we wanna image this charge motion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1748960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The video is a simulation, but it's been \nvalidated by the experiments done at SLAC."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1753760,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our method for probing these seems to work. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1755760,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can compare to a handful of points \nand say, oh, these look broadly similar. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1759840,
    "dDurationMs": 6618,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Much after this few femtosecond, as we approach \nfive to 10 femtoseconds, we start to diverge. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1766458,
    "dDurationMs": 2742,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our prediction starts to \ndiverge from our measurement. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1769200,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And actually this is the most \nexciting time in science, right? "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1771520,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you have a prediction, and \nthen you have a measurement,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1773840,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they don't agree, that's \nwhen you get really excited, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1776320,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you just found something \nyou didn't know ahead of time. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1779040,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You couldn't have predicted that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1780480,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think the most powerful thing for me here \nis we animate a lot of electrons, right? "
    } ]
  }, {
